  "goodToKnow": "Der Verkehrsminister (die Verkehrsministerin) is the transport minister, responsible for roads, railways, aviation and shipping. The federal post is often in the spotlight over Deutsche Bahn's problems, the Autobahn speed limit debate and the failed car toll (Pkw-Maut), which the EU Court struck down in 2019, costing taxpayers hundreds of millions. Der Verkehr means traffic. Plural: die Verkehrsminister."
